Nit: ints are still 32 bits on most 64-bit systems ( http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/64-bit#Specific_data_models )
Example:
  mrj10@mjlap:~$ uname -m
  x86_64
  mrj10@mjlap:~$ cat test.c
  #include <stdio.h>
  int main()
  {
    printf("%zu\n",sizeof(int));
    return 0;  
  }
  mrj10@mjlap:~$ gcc test.c -o test
  mrj10@mjlap:~$ ./test
  4
